  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the primary uncertainty is whether RNA data alone carries sufficient signal for the task and what baseline performance looks like. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most interpretable configuration: it uses a standard linear encoder (PCA), a single profile, and no image or fusion components, so any observed performance can be cleanly attributed to the raw RNA signal with minimal processing. Establishing this baseline is essential before evaluating more complex choices (learned encoders, multiprofile aggregation, image modality, or fusion strategies), because it provides the reference against which all subsequent design decisions—encoder choice, profile aggregation, modality combination, and fusion method—can be measured. It is the highest-information first experiment under a limited budget because it anchors the entire comparison space with minimal confounding variables."
}

